1
00:00:01,270 --> 00:00:08,150
The new morning we've finally found

2
00:00:01,270 --> 00:00:08,150
Yatto mitsuketa atarashii asa wa

3
00:00:08,150 --> 00:00:12,190
is being hampered by the past.

4
00:00:08,150 --> 00:00:12,190
Tsukihi ga jama wo suru

5
00:00:12,390 --> 00:00:17,660
What we chased after wasn't the future,

6
00:00:12,390 --> 00:00:17,660
Mukau saki wa tsugi ja nakute

7
00:00:17,660 --> 00:00:21,490
but the past so full of remorse.

8
00:00:17,660 --> 00:00:21,490
Sugi bakari oikaketa

9
00:00:22,870 --> 00:00:27,960
The ruthless memories won't stop playing;

10
00:00:22,870 --> 00:00:27,960
Nariyamanai yousha nai omoide tachi wa

11
00:00:27,960 --> 00:00:32,050
they won't be forgiving us for a long time.

12
00:00:27,960 --> 00:00:32,050
Yurushite kuresou nimonai

13
00:00:33,340 --> 00:00:37,890
It's about now that a teardrop

14
00:00:33,340 --> 00:00:37,890
Sorosoro kana tesaguri tsukareta hoho wo

15
00:00:37,890 --> 00:00:42,560
beings to roll down my fatigued cheeks.

16
00:00:37,890 --> 00:00:42,560
Kattou ga koboreochiru

17
00:00:42,890 --> 00:00:47,810
Will this rain ever stop?

18
00:00:42,890 --> 00:00:47,810
Ame wa itsuka yamunodeshouka

19
00:00:47,810 --> 00:00:53,030
I've been freezing for a long time.

20
00:00:47,810 --> 00:00:53,030
Zuibun nagai aida tsumetai

21
00:00:53,030 --> 00:00:58,320
Why does the rain continue to fix on me?

22
00:00:53,030 --> 00:00:58,320
Ame wa doushite boku wo erabuno

23
00:00:58,320 --> 00:01:03,080
I wonder if it could embrace me.

24
00:00:58,320 --> 00:01:03,080
Tsutsumarete iikana

25
00:01:03,080 --> 00:01:07,870
Today, the rain falls again;

26
00:01:03,080 --> 00:01:07,870
Ame wa yamu koto wo shirazuni

27
00:01:07,870 --> 00:01:13,090
endlessly it falls knowing no end.

28
00:01:07,870 --> 00:01:13,090
Kyou mo furitsuzukukeredo

29
00:01:13,090 --> 00:01:18,130
We nestle close to each other to share the warmth

30
00:01:13,090 --> 00:01:18,130
Sotto sashidashita kasa no naka de

31
00:01:18,680 --> 00:01:29,850
under this umbrella, you gently held out to me.

32
00:01:18,680 --> 00:01:29,850
Nukumori ni yorisoinagara

33
00:01:40,240 --> 00:01:41,320
Bastard!

34
00:02:00,390 --> 00:02:03,180
That's as far as you're going to get.

35
00:02:03,200 --> 00:02:06,200
A Fierce Counterattack

36
00:02:03,200 --> 00:02:06,200
A Fierce Counterattack

37
00:02:11,940 --> 00:02:13,320
Dad!

38
00:02:13,320 --> 00:02:17,440
He was trying to make philosopher's stones again.

39
00:02:17,860 --> 00:02:20,700
Humans should just stay as stones.

40
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:26,450
Why do you treat humans like such lowly creatures?

41
00:02:27,160 --> 00:02:29,830
Philosopher's stones can be created from humans,

42
00:02:29,830 --> 00:02:32,540
and homunculi can be created from philosopher's stones.

43
00:02:32,540 --> 00:02:35,300
So, answer me. What can be created from homunculi?

44
00:02:35,300 --> 00:02:36,840
What do you give birth to?!

45
00:02:37,300 --> 00:02:40,970
An existence that only brings about destruction can be called 'God'?

46
00:02:41,380 --> 00:02:44,050
You may believe that you've become a perfect being,

47
00:02:44,390 --> 00:02:46,890
but all you are is an obstacle in the cycle of life!

48
00:02:48,680 --> 00:02:50,100
Is that so?

49
00:02:50,100 --> 00:02:51,980
Then I shall give birth to humans.

50
00:03:18,420 --> 00:03:20,840
I've obtained immortality....

51
00:03:21,510 --> 00:03:24,930
I'm still alive...

52
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:27,930
King Xerxes!

53
00:03:42,240 --> 00:03:43,200
A body!

54
00:03:43,200 --> 00:03:44,490
This body is mine!

55
00:03:44,490 --> 00:03:45,780
Finally, a body...

56
00:03:45,780 --> 00:03:46,620
Stop...

57
00:03:46,620 --> 00:03:47,490
Please, stop...

58
00:03:47,950 --> 00:03:50,540
This... This isn't right!

59
00:03:51,660 --> 00:03:53,790
Look! A body!

60
00:03:53,790 --> 00:03:55,080
Hohenheim...

61
00:03:55,540 --> 00:03:56,960
Guys...

62
00:03:58,550 --> 00:04:01,510
You!!

63
00:04:10,890 --> 00:04:11,770
Shoot!

64
00:04:17,980 --> 00:04:19,860
What the hell is going on?!

65
00:04:23,530 --> 00:04:24,820
Shit!

66
00:04:24,820 --> 00:04:25,740
Greed!

67
00:04:26,240 --> 00:04:27,490
D.K.!

68
00:04:27,490 --> 00:04:28,240
Looks like you're okay.

69
00:04:28,580 --> 00:04:31,200
Great timing! Give me a ride.

70
00:04:31,200 --> 00:04:33,370
It'll probably help to have someone with you who knows what's up.

71
00:04:33,370 --> 00:04:36,330
Yeah! What on earth is going on?!

72
00:04:36,330 --> 00:04:40,000
The leader of the homunculi, "Father," is off on a rampage.

73
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:43,170
Those who can't fight should get off right here!

74
00:04:44,130 --> 00:04:45,010
Hey!

75
00:04:45,010 --> 00:04:46,970
The frog and the two princesses!

76
00:04:46,970 --> 00:04:47,800
Scram!

77
00:04:47,800 --> 00:04:49,220
You're all injured!

78
00:04:49,760 --> 00:04:51,100
Don't be ridiculous!

79
00:04:51,100 --> 00:04:53,140
Who else but me will take the lead?!

80
00:04:53,350 --> 00:04:54,600
Hell if I know!

81
00:04:54,600 --> 00:04:55,980
Just get the hell off of there!

82
00:04:55,980 --> 00:04:58,350
This ain't the time to be blabbering on about leading!

83
00:04:58,560 --> 00:04:59,860
You have no right to-

84
00:04:59,860 --> 00:05:00,650
General!

85
00:05:01,940 --> 00:05:03,440
A call from headquarters.

86
00:05:04,530 --> 00:05:06,700
Mission headquarters? It's me.

87
00:05:06,700 --> 00:05:08,070
What's the status over there?

88
00:05:08,910 --> 00:05:11,740
Ma'am, half of Central Headquarters...

89
00:05:12,990 --> 00:05:14,750
...has been annihilated.

90
00:05:15,910 --> 00:05:17,210
What?

91
00:05:17,210 --> 00:05:19,290
We can't get in touch with the North Gate.

92
00:05:21,710 --> 00:05:23,630
That's what he's capable of.

93
00:05:25,970 --> 00:05:27,840
Just what is he...?

94
00:05:27,840 --> 00:05:29,930
He looks like an ordinary human from the outside.

95
00:05:30,430 --> 00:05:35,310
However, he has several hundred thousand human souls worth of philosopher's stones stored in his body,

96
00:05:35,310 --> 00:05:38,810
and has absorbed God with that energy.

97
00:05:40,150 --> 00:05:43,150
You alchemists out there should understand the severity of the situation.

98
00:05:43,860 --> 00:05:45,320
Philosopher's stones...

99
00:05:45,650 --> 00:05:48,070
You ordinary humans should stay behind.

100
00:05:49,160 --> 00:05:53,120
My men are up there fighting.

101
00:05:53,120 --> 00:05:55,830
I am their commander.

102
00:05:58,670 --> 00:06:01,790
General, headquarters would like to speak with you.

103
00:06:04,130 --> 00:06:05,260
What is it?

104
00:06:05,260 --> 00:06:06,590
Don't worry, General.

105
00:06:07,130 --> 00:06:14,720
Don't forget that we Briggs soldiers are capable of operating even if our boss is absent.

106
00:06:14,720 --> 00:06:17,100
Armory, Team Yellow! Are you alive?!

107
00:06:17,100 --> 00:06:19,350
East Gate, Team Blue! Come in!

108
00:06:20,060 --> 00:06:22,860
We overheard that you're injured.

109
00:06:22,860 --> 00:06:25,570
Please watch over us from there.

110
00:06:28,440 --> 00:06:29,400
Alex!

111
00:06:29,400 --> 00:06:29,860
Ma'am!

112
00:06:31,070 --> 00:06:32,660
Bring the communications equipment!

113
00:06:34,240 --> 00:06:35,540
Win no matter what!

114
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:38,790
Of course we will!

115
00:06:39,330 --> 00:06:41,460
Right. Let's go, Lieutenant.

116
00:06:41,460 --> 00:06:44,840
Hey! Both of you are hurt!

117
00:06:44,840 --> 00:06:47,670
I'll burn his philosopher's stone to a crisp.

118
00:06:48,340 --> 00:06:50,880
But in order for me to do that, I'll need the lieutenant's help.

119
00:06:52,720 --> 00:06:54,300
Who cares, let's get a move on.

120
00:06:56,600 --> 00:06:59,350
My duty is to protect the young master.

121
00:07:04,770 --> 00:07:05,770
Please take care of Izumi...

122
00:07:06,520 --> 00:07:07,650
...and everyone else.

123
00:07:10,650 --> 00:07:15,160
Let's rock 'n' roll!!

124
00:07:37,310 --> 00:07:39,270
So this is where he bit the dust.

125
00:07:40,600 --> 00:07:41,890
Did you do this?

126
00:07:42,440 --> 00:07:46,730
He was heavily injured by the time he got here.

127
00:07:46,730 --> 00:07:49,400
If that hadn't been the case, I'm not sure whether I would have made it out alive.

128
00:07:50,740 --> 00:07:56,780
Captain Buccaneer dealt a fatal blow to Bradley with the aid of a man from Xing...

129
00:08:03,370 --> 00:08:04,790
So, Bradley...

130
00:08:05,710 --> 00:08:07,790
...wouldn't you say my men were quite something?

131
00:08:34,320 --> 00:08:37,490
Shao May, you're all right...

132
00:08:37,490 --> 00:08:38,780
Thank goodness...

133
00:08:45,870 --> 00:08:47,040
Sir Alphonse?!

134
00:08:52,840 --> 00:08:54,050
May...

135
00:08:54,050 --> 00:08:57,010
I'm glad you're alive...

136
00:08:57,220 --> 00:08:59,300
Sir Alphonse, your body...!

137
00:09:04,980 --> 00:09:06,560
Sir Alphonse!

138
00:09:09,270 --> 00:09:12,400
Oh no! If you hadn't protected me...!

139
00:09:12,940 --> 00:09:14,690
Sir Alphonse!

140
00:09:14,690 --> 00:09:16,450
Sir Alphonse!!

141
00:09:34,920 --> 00:09:36,050
Master!

142
00:09:36,300 --> 00:09:38,510
Master! Master!!

143
00:09:39,510 --> 00:09:40,720
I'm still alive...

144
00:09:42,390 --> 00:09:46,560
Mr. Hohenheim protected us...

145
00:09:51,560 --> 00:09:54,110
H-Hohenheim!

146
00:09:56,110 --> 00:09:58,150
Hey! Hang in there!

147
00:10:12,130 --> 00:10:13,340
Hohenheim!!

148
00:10:13,500 --> 00:10:15,300
Two to start with.

149
00:10:20,050 --> 00:10:21,220
Stop it!!

150
00:10:30,480 --> 00:10:32,900
Our target is a man with long, blonde hair!

151
00:10:32,900 --> 00:10:35,360
Don't confuse him with the Fullmetal Alchemist!

152
00:10:35,360 --> 00:10:36,030
Roger!

153
00:10:36,860 --> 00:10:38,280
East Gate, Team Blue! Step on it!

154
00:10:38,780 --> 00:10:41,610
West Gate, Team White! Get in the shadows of the west building of headquarters!

155
00:10:41,610 --> 00:10:42,660
Yes, sir!

156
00:10:43,870 --> 00:10:44,910
Master!

157
00:10:54,380 --> 00:10:55,290
Fire!!

158
00:11:07,010 --> 00:11:09,350
Yo, Fullmetal! You alive?

159
00:11:09,810 --> 00:11:11,980
Attacks like these won't even scratch him!

160
00:11:12,900 --> 00:11:13,810
You're kidding me!

161
00:11:19,610 --> 00:11:21,610
Don't give him a chance to counterattack!

162
00:11:22,240 --> 00:11:23,240
Aye, sir!

163
00:11:33,710 --> 00:11:36,790
Dammit! He looks like he's enjoying the breeze!

164
00:11:36,790 --> 00:11:38,210
Roger that!

165
00:11:38,210 --> 00:11:39,170
Put me through to each squadron.

166
00:11:40,800 --> 00:11:42,050
Is that so?!

167
00:11:42,050 --> 00:11:44,180
Cease fire! Duck!

168
00:12:15,880 --> 00:12:17,080
Did I hit him?

169
00:12:17,080 --> 00:12:18,960
Grazed him.

170
00:12:18,960 --> 00:12:20,500
Fix your aim towards 12 o'clock.

171
00:12:21,960 --> 00:12:23,970
I can't see, so I don't know how much I should suppress my flames.

172
00:12:24,550 --> 00:12:26,760
Don't suppress them at all!

173
00:12:26,760 --> 00:12:27,800
Distance 50...

174
00:12:27,800 --> 00:12:29,140
No, 53!

175
00:12:29,680 --> 00:12:32,730
I still can't get used to this clapping business.

176
00:12:39,820 --> 00:12:41,690
A frontal attack!

177
00:12:45,150 --> 00:12:46,240
Nice work!

178
00:12:46,660 --> 00:12:48,950
Take that back. It's pretty useful.

179
00:12:49,410 --> 00:12:50,740
Fire! Fire!

180
00:12:50,740 --> 00:12:51,910
Keep it up!

181
00:12:52,700 --> 00:12:55,460
Don't give him the chance to counterattack!

182
00:12:55,460 --> 00:12:58,170
Keep making him use up his philosopher's stone!

183
00:13:23,690 --> 00:13:24,990
Incredible!

184
00:13:24,990 --> 00:13:29,200
I could make the world mine if I had that power!

185
00:13:29,200 --> 00:13:30,870
Hey, Greed!

186
00:13:31,450 --> 00:13:35,620
Is this what you meant by "making the world yours"?

187
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:37,160
That's right!

188
00:13:37,160 --> 00:13:40,880
If I could just obtain that, the entire world would be mine!

189
00:13:41,420 --> 00:13:45,010
This feeling of emptiness inside me might just be cured!

190
00:13:45,300 --> 00:13:49,640
The thirst that's been haunting me since birth just might be quenched!

191
00:13:50,090 --> 00:13:51,720
You're disgraceful, Greed.

192
00:13:52,220 --> 00:13:54,270
That's not what you really want.

193
00:13:56,430 --> 00:13:58,600
Keep your mouth shut, shitty brat!

194
00:13:59,400 --> 00:14:01,690
I'm Greed, the avaricious!

195
00:14:01,690 --> 00:14:04,190
I'll obtain everything I want at any cost!

196
00:14:08,570 --> 00:14:09,990
Homunculus Cake, anyone?

197
00:14:22,750 --> 00:14:24,500
Not even a scratch...

198
00:14:25,880 --> 00:14:28,510
We need to do something about that barrier!

199
00:14:28,970 --> 00:14:31,010
We're running out of ammo! Bring us some more!

200
00:14:31,260 --> 00:14:32,760
Futile acts.

201
00:14:33,510 --> 00:14:37,020
Mere humans can hardly lay a finger on me.

202
00:14:40,020 --> 00:14:43,360
If humans can't, what about a homunculus?!

203
00:14:47,860 --> 00:14:50,280
Great timing, Greed.

204
00:14:50,280 --> 00:14:52,740
You're such a good son.

205
00:14:52,740 --> 00:14:56,200
I was just in need of a philosopher's stone.

206
00:14:57,240 --> 00:14:58,870
I'll be taking yours.

207
00:15:10,510 --> 00:15:11,590
Just kidding.

208
00:15:12,590 --> 00:15:16,310
You can't take my philosopher's stone without putting your barrier down, right?

209
00:15:16,310 --> 00:15:21,810
Did you not consider the possibility that you'd have the power of God taken from you instead?

210
00:15:23,980 --> 00:15:26,650
I'll take all of it!

211
00:15:33,280 --> 00:15:34,870
Greed!

212
00:16:01,520 --> 00:16:03,310
Don't give up!

213
00:16:15,780 --> 00:16:18,490
He... blocked it himself.

214
00:16:23,540 --> 00:16:25,000
He's at his limit!

215
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:33,260
He can no longer hold down God!

216
00:17:11,500 --> 00:17:12,760
Stone...!

217
00:17:12,760 --> 00:17:13,880
Stone!

218
00:17:14,510 --> 00:17:16,340
Philosopher's stone!

219
00:17:30,610 --> 00:17:32,360
Run, Edward!

220
00:17:32,820 --> 00:17:34,860
Brother, run!

221
00:17:34,860 --> 00:17:36,450
Brother!!

222
00:17:39,700 --> 00:17:41,370
Stop it!

223
00:17:41,370 --> 00:17:42,740
Dammit!!

224
00:17:44,080 --> 00:17:45,040
Sir Al!

225
00:17:46,540 --> 00:17:47,620
Stop...!

226
00:17:47,620 --> 00:17:48,830
Stop it!

227
00:17:49,580 --> 00:17:51,040
Help...

228
00:17:51,040 --> 00:17:52,250
Help him...!

229
00:17:52,250 --> 00:17:54,050
Help my-

230
00:18:06,100 --> 00:18:08,440
May, I need you to do me a favor.

231
00:18:09,480 --> 00:18:14,070
Brother got my soul back by sacrificing his right arm.

232
00:18:15,230 --> 00:18:18,240
In that case, it should be possible to do the opposite.

233
00:18:19,910 --> 00:18:21,740
Sir Alphonse...?

234
00:18:23,240 --> 00:18:24,990
All I need you to do is to make a path.

235
00:18:25,580 --> 00:18:27,000
You can do it, right?

236
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:29,370
But if I did that, you'd...!

237
00:18:29,370 --> 00:18:30,920
We're running out of time!

238
00:18:30,920 --> 00:18:31,750
Please.

239
00:18:33,250 --> 00:18:36,380
You're the only one I can ask to do something like this.

240
00:18:44,140 --> 00:18:45,260
Stone...

241
00:18:45,390 --> 00:18:47,180
Human...

242
00:18:47,600 --> 00:18:49,020
Energy...!

243
00:18:49,020 --> 00:18:50,270
Edward!!

244
00:18:50,270 --> 00:18:52,940
Give it to me!!

245
00:19:07,200 --> 00:19:08,700
What are you trying to do...?

246
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:11,500
Cut it out...

247
00:19:11,500 --> 00:19:12,420
Hey...

248
00:19:12,830 --> 00:19:13,790
Al!

249
00:19:15,790 --> 00:19:17,920
Win this, Brother.

250
00:19:18,670 --> 00:19:21,800
Don't do it!!!

251
00:19:38,150 --> 00:19:40,240
Was that enough for you?

252
00:19:40,490 --> 00:19:41,320
Yeah.

253
00:19:41,860 --> 00:19:43,740
All that's left for me to do now is to believe in him.

254
00:20:14,850 --> 00:20:17,860
Yo. Looks like you got your soul back.

255
00:20:19,070 --> 00:20:21,860
Think he'll come here to bring you back?

256
00:20:23,070 --> 00:20:25,110
He will. I know he will.

257
00:20:31,540 --> 00:20:34,580
I'm curious to see what he'll sacrifice to do so.

258
00:20:46,140 --> 00:20:49,010
You idiot!!

259
00:21:17,920 --> 00:21:18,920
It's working.

260
00:21:19,590 --> 00:21:21,840
He... He has a chance!

261
00:21:21,840 --> 00:21:22,500
Keep it up!

262
00:21:22,500 --> 00:21:23,710
Kiddo!!

263
00:21:23,710 --> 00:21:24,970
That's the spirit!

264
00:21:24,970 --> 00:21:26,380
Get him, kid!

265
00:21:26,380 --> 00:21:27,470
Rush in!

266
00:21:27,630 --> 00:21:28,840
Edward!

267
00:21:28,840 --> 00:21:29,390
Ed!

268
00:21:29,390 --> 00:21:31,220
Edward Elric!

269
00:21:31,220 --> 00:21:35,270
Go!!

270
00:21:38,270 --> 00:21:39,230
Greed.

271
00:21:40,440 --> 00:21:42,400
Isn't this...

272
00:21:43,480 --> 00:21:44,650
...what you've always wanted more than anything?

273
00:21:45,190 --> 00:21:46,400
Mr. Edward!

274
00:21:46,570 --> 00:21:47,650
Edward!

275
00:21:47,990 --> 00:21:48,660
Go!

276
00:21:49,360 --> 00:21:50,410
Fullmetal!

277
00:21:52,280 --> 00:21:54,160
Yeah, you're right on target.

278
00:21:55,410 --> 00:21:57,620
What I've always wanted...

279
00:22:02,540 --> 00:22:05,510
...are friends like these.

280
00:22:19,730 --> 00:22:21,560
Get up, punk!

281
00:22:23,320 --> 00:22:28,070
I'll show you the difference between us!

282
00:22:39,250 --> 00:22:42,800
Ever since that day passed,

283
00:22:39,250 --> 00:22:42,800
Ano hi kara zutto

284
00:22:42,800 --> 00:22:47,050
I promised myself that I'd never cry.

285
00:22:42,800 --> 00:22:47,050
Nakanaito kimetekitakedo

286
00:22:47,590 --> 00:22:52,600
But even while I hoarded up the pain,

287
00:22:47,590 --> 00:22:52,600
Itami wo kasanetemo

288
00:22:52,600 --> 00:22:57,710
there was something I couldn't forgive myself for.

289
00:22:52,600 --> 00:22:57,710
Nanika wo yurusezu ni ita

290
00:22:59,190 --> 00:23:01,150
I'll never be able

291
00:22:59,190 --> 00:23:01,150
Mou modorenai

292
00:23:01,150 --> 00:23:03,650
to return to those days.

293
00:23:01,150 --> 00:23:03,650
Ikutsumo no hibi

294
00:23:03,650 --> 00:23:08,740
I'm still powerless.

295
00:23:03,650 --> 00:23:08,740
Boku wa mada nanimo dekizuni

296
00:23:08,740 --> 00:23:13,990
I watch as the shards of memories disappear, one by one;

297
00:23:08,740 --> 00:23:13,990
Kimi no ita kioku no kakera

298
00:23:13,990 --> 00:23:19,860
memories of when you were still with me.

299
00:23:13,990 --> 00:23:19,860
Mata hitotsu kieteyuku

300
00:23:20,540 --> 00:23:22,880
I long to become

301
00:23:20,540 --> 00:23:22,880
Kyou yori motto

302
00:23:22,880 --> 00:23:25,630
stronger than I am now,

303
00:23:22,880 --> 00:23:25,630
Tsuyoku naritai

304
00:23:25,630 --> 00:23:30,770
so that my voice will eventually reach you.

305
00:23:25,630 --> 00:23:30,770
Kono koe ga itsuka todokuyouni

306
00:23:30,770 --> 00:23:33,140
If the wind happens to stop

307
00:23:30,770 --> 00:23:33,140
Arukitsuzukete

308
00:23:33,140 --> 00:23:35,850
in the midst of my long journey,

309
00:23:33,140 --> 00:23:35,850
Kaze ga yandara

310
00:23:35,850 --> 00:23:40,560
I'll look up at the sky in search of you.

311
00:23:35,850 --> 00:23:40,560
Kimi wo sagashite sora miageruyo

312
00:23:41,310 --> 00:23:47,900
Beyond the daybreak, a ray of light breaks free.

313
00:23:41,310 --> 00:23:47,900
Yoake no saki ni hikari ga sasuyo

314
00:23:49,070 --> 00:23:53,450
A rainbow spans across the sky.

315
00:23:49,070 --> 00:23:53,450
Niji ga kakaruyo

316
00:24:01,120 --> 00:24:05,790
His power could bring anything about.

317
00:24:05,790 --> 00:24:08,250
However, he does not hesitate.

318
00:24:08,250 --> 00:24:11,090
Not when it is to protect the ones he loves.

319
00:24:12,220 --> 00:24:16,350
Next time, Fullmetal Alchemist:

320
00:24:16,350 --> 00:24:20,870
Episode 63, The Other Side of the Gateway.

321
00:24:16,370 --> 00:24:20,870
 The Other Side 
of the Gateway

322
00:24:21,690 --> 00:24:26,400
He fades away after overseeing all.
